[' I'll provide a high-level design and code snippets for the given programming task. Due to the complexity of the task, I'll focus on key components and interfaces.

1. Microservice Interface:

```java
public interface Microservice {
    void start();
    void stop();
    int getMaxRequests();
    int processRequest();
}
```

2. LoadBalancer Interface:

```java
public interface LoadBalancer {
    List<Microservice> getActiveServices();
    Microservice chooseService(List<Microservice> services);
}
```

3. ServiceManager:

```java
import java.util.*;

public class ServiceManager implements LoadBalancer {
    private final Map<String, Microservice> services = new HashMap<>();

    public void registerService(String id, Microservice service) {
        services.put(id, service);
    }

    public void unregisterService(String id) {
        services.remove(id);
    }

    @Override
    public List<Microservice> getActiveServices() {
        return new ArrayList<>(services.values());
    }

    @Override
    public Microservice chooseService(List<Microservice> services) {
        if (services.isEmpty()) return null;

        Microservice chosen = services.get(0);
        for (Microservice service : services) {
            if (service.processRequest() >= chosen.getMaxRequests()) {
                chosen = service;
            }
        }
        return chosen;
    }
}
```

4. RequestRouter:

```java
public class RequestRouter implements Runnable {
    private final LoadBalancer loadBalancer;
    private final BlockingQueue<Runnable> tasks = new LinkedBlockingQueue<>();

    public RequestRouter(LoadBalancer loadBalancer) {
        this.loadBalancer = loadBalancer;
    }

    public void submitTask(Runnable task) {
        tasks.add(task);
    }

    @Override
    public void run() {
        while (true) {
            Microservice service = loadBalancer.chooseService(loadBalancer.getActiveServices());
            if (service != null) {
                service.start();
                Runnable task = tasks.take();
                service.processRequest();
                service.stop();
                task.run();
            }
        }
    }
}
```

5. ScalingManager:

