[' Here's a Java code snippet that implements the given programming task:

```java
import java.io.*;
import java.lang.reflect.InvocationTargetException;
import java.util.*;
import java.nio.file.Files;
import java.nio.file.Path;
import java.nio.file.StandardOpenOption;

class Event implements Serializable {
    private static final long serialVersionUID = 1L;
    String type;
    // Add other event properties as needed
}

class EventTypeFilter implements Filter<Event> {
    private final String targetType;

    public EventTypeFilter(String targetType) {
        this.targetType = targetType;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean accept(Event event) {
        return event.type.equals(targetType);
    }
}

public List<Event> processLogFile(Path logFilePath, String targetType) throws IOException, ClassNotFoundException, InstantiationException, IllegalAccessException, InvocationTargetException {
    List<Event> events = new ArrayList<>();
    int index = 0;
    ObjectInputStream ois = null;
    try (BufferedReader reader = Files.newBufferedReader(logFilePath)) {
        String line;
        while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
            try {
                ois = new ObjectInputStream(new ByteArrayInputStream(line.getBytes()));
                Event event = (Event) ois.readObject();
                if (new EventTypeFilter(targetType).accept(event)) {
                    events.add(event);
                }
            } catch (ClassNotFoundException e) {
                System.err.println("Failed to deserialize entry at index " + index + ", type: " + event.getClass().getName());
            } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException | InstantiationException | IllegalAccessException | InvocationTargetException e) {
                System.err.println("Error while processing entry at index " + index);
                e.printStackTrace();
            } finally {
                if (ois != null) ois.close();
            }
            index++;
        }
    }
    return events;
}
```

This code defines an `Event` class that represents a serialized event in the log file, and a method `processLogFile()` that reads the log file line by line, deserializes each event using ObjectInputStream, filters the events based on the provided target type, and handles exceptions gracefully. The method uses a streaming approach to handle potentially infinite log files efficiently.

The code also includes a simple report of failed entries due to missing classes or other errors during processing. To ensure long-term maintainability, the system scales well under varying loads by choosing appropriate data structures and algorithms.']

