Now, let's implement the email update method:

```java
@Service
public class EmailService {

    @Autowired
    private UserRepository userRepository;

    @Autowired
    private ExternalIdentityService externalIdentityService;

    @Autowired
    private Cache cache;

    @Autowired
    private MfaAuthenticationManager mfaAuthenticationManager;

    public void updateEmail(Long userId, String newEmail) {
        User user = userRepository.findById(userId).orElseThrow(() -> new RuntimeException("User not found"));

        if (!isMaintenanceWindow()) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Update attempt outside of maintenance window");
        }

        // Validate email uniqueness within the system
        if (userRepository.findByEmailIgnoreCase(newEmail).stream().filter(u -> !u.getId().equals(userId)).findFirst().isPresent()) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Email already in use");
        }

        // Verify user's current email with the external identity service
        String currentEmail = externalIdentityService.getUserEmail(user.getEmail());
        if (!currentEmail.equals(user.getEmail())) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Invalid current email");
        }

        // Implement exponential backoff for network failures
        int attempts = 0;
        do {
            try {
                mfaAuthenticationManager.authenticateUser(user, MFA_AUTHENTICATION_TYPE);
                user.setEmail(newEmail);
                userRepository.save(user);
                logAttempt("Successful email update");
                break;
            } catch (Exception e) {
                attempts++;
                if (attempts >= MAX_ATTEMPTS) {
                    throw new RuntimeException("Maximum retries exceeded", e);
                }
                // Exponential backoff strategy: wait for 2^n seconds before the next attempt
                try {
                    Thread.sleep(Math.pow(2, attempts) * BACKOFF_FACTOR);
                } catch (InterruptedException e1) {
                    throw new RuntimeException("Failed to sleep during backoff", e1);
                }
            }
        } while (true);
    }
}
```

In this example, `UserRepository`, `ExternalIdentityService`, `MfaAuthenticationManager`, and `logAttempt` are placeholders for your actual implementations. You should also define the constants `MFA_AUTHENTICATION_TYPE`, `MAX_ATTEMPTS`, and `BACKOFF_FACTOR`.

